Batsie — reference only, no code incorporated
https://github.com/leptos-null/Batsie
================================================================================

`Core/Sensors/BatteryCenterBridge.swift` follows the real `BCBatteryDevice`
interface rather than guesswork, and two details of loading BatteryCenter from
a sandboxed app — using NSBundle rather than dlopen, and prefixing the path
with DYLD_ROOT_PATH so the same code works in the simulator — were learned
from reading Batsie. No source from that project is reproduced here.


================================================================================
CellularInfo — reference only, no code incorporated
https://github.com/DevelopCubeLab/CellularInfo
================================================================================

`Sources/DeviceControl/BandInfo.swift` and the band read/write shape in
`Sources/DeviceControl/CommCenterBridge.m` implement the same feature as
CellularInfo, and the following were learned from reading it:

  * which CoreTelephony calls carry band information, and that a write replaces
    only the "active" set while the "supported" set is carried back untouched;
  * the band-number spellings per radio access technology (n78 / B3 / BC0 /
    plain integers) and the fact that a radio-access-technology key has to be
    matched by substring, with TDSCDMA tested before CDMA.

No source from that project is reproduced here. The implementation is written
for this repository: it models a radio access technology as a value wrapping
the original dictionary key rather than as a fixed enum, so an unrecognised
technology is preserved instead of dropped.

CellularInfo itself is licensed under the GNU GPL v3. It is listed here because
its API facts were read from it, not because any of it was copied — the same
arrangement as the Batsie entry above. Keeping GPL-3.0 code out of this repository is
deliberate; see README.md.

